WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.556
Classify information before moving it into a rented environment.

00:00:04.556 --> 00:00:12.149
Prompts and uploaded documents may contain credentials, personal records, source code, intellectual property, or regulated data.

00:00:12.149 --> 00:00:16.270
Model files may have license or distribution restrictions.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:21.694
Logs can reproduce prompt content, file paths, tokens, and request metadata.

00:00:21.694 --> 00:00:28.853
Confirm that the provider, account, region, and service type are approved for the data involved.

00:00:28.853 --> 00:00:34.276
Use identity and access management to grant the minimum permissions needed.

00:00:34.276 --> 00:00:37.530
Separate human administration from application identities.

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:45.123
Protect SSH keys, rotate stale access, and restrict firewall rules to known sources and required ports.

00:00:45.123 --> 00:00:54.018
A notebook, dashboard, or inference server should not be exposed publicly without authentication simply because the rental is temporary.

00:00:54.018 --> 00:01:04.214
Store API keys, repository tokens, and credentials in a secrets mechanism, not in shell history, notebooks, container images, or shared setup notes.

00:01:04.214 --> 00:01:09.637
Encrypt disks, object storage, snapshots, and network traffic according to policy.

00:01:09.637 --> 00:01:15.929
Minimize prompt logging, set retention periods, and control who can inspect operational data.

00:01:15.929 --> 00:01:23.088
Security responsibility remains with the renter even when the underlying hardware belongs to the provider.

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:25.474
Plan deletion before upload.

00:01:25.474 --> 00:01:35.670
At session end, remove temporary files, revoke short-lived credentials, and determine whether disks, snapshots, model caches, logs, object versions, or backups remain.

00:01:35.670 --> 00:01:44.565
Deleting an instance may not delete associated storage, while marketplace hosts may have different erasure assurances than major providers.

00:01:44.565 --> 00:01:47.819
Record what was retained and why.

00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:51.941
A clean teardown protects both privacy and cost.
